# As correlate-gnn, with a filter restart (correlate.md, Restart) when a report
# is far outside its track's prediction: d² of 200 or more.
# Derived values, each from a stated probability or unit:
# - course 42 deg and speed 73 %: each track's velocity
#   error is vel_sigma_ms = 5 m/s per axis, so the difference of two tracks has
#   5 * sqrt(2) = 7.1 m/s, and 99 % of it (z = 2.576) lies within 18.2 m/s.
#   At 25 m/s that is 18.2 / 25 = 0.73 rad (42 deg) of course and a
#   speed ratio within 73 %. Below 5 m/s, the velocity error itself, course
#   is not defined, so both tests are skipped; between 5 and 25 m/s the tests
#   are stricter than 99 %.
# - height within 300 m: three times a 100 m height error.
# - confirm on 2 reports in a row: a different object passes the 99 % gate by
#   chance at most about one time in ten here, so two in a row keep false
#   confirmation near 1 %. Leave after 2 failures in a row of the 99.99 %
#   region, so one outlier report never splits a pair.
# - stale after 120 s without a report (the fixed form of staleness): ten
#   times the slowest update period this pack expects (12 s); ten missed
#   updates in a row at a detection probability of 0.5 happen about 0.1 % of
#   the time. (Staleness from each source's rate, stale_rate, measured worse
#   for this pack on the benchmark, so it is not used here.)
pack           correlate-gnn-restart
version        1.0.0
filter         accel_var=1 default_ce_m=50 vel_sigma_ms=5 unknown_vel_ms=100
gate           mahalanobis gate=9.21
gate           same key=track.simulated
gate           same key=@env
confirm        course max_deg=42 min_speed_ms=5
confirm        speed max_pct=73 min_speed_ms=5
confirm        altitude max_m=300
confirm_count  2
hold           mahalanobis gate=18.42
hold_failures  2
stale_ms       120000
same_source    forbid
output         priority
restart        gate=200
